// Reproduces registry.gno:149's "Service Not Found" sentence with a backtick
// in the caller-controlled address segment. InlineText escapes the backtick to
// \`, a backslash is literal inside a code span, so the span closes early and
// the stray backtick pairs with the next one in the sentence.
// Measured at 7c41a297d against gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown.
//
// Run: from a gno checkout:
//   gh pr checkout 5871 -R gnolang/gno && git checkout 7c41a297d
//   cp <this file> gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown/golden/sanitize/
//   go test ./gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown/ -run TestSanitizeIntegration
//   rm gno.land/pkg/gnoweb/markdown/golden/sanitize/inline-code-span-breakout.txtar

// MARKDOWNFUNC: InlineText
// CONTEXT: No service with address `%s` and name `svc` is registered.
-- input.md --
g1`evil
-- output.md --
g1\`evil
-- output.html --
<p>No service with address <code>g1\</code>evil<code>and name</code>svc` is registered.</p>
